  "name": "Example: Subtracting a Positive Number From a Smaller Positive Number",
  "problem": "Luisa has an overdraft facility authorized by her bank. Her bank balance on Monday was $\\[math] 173.25.$ On Tuesday, Luisa decided to withdraw $\\[/math] 250.70$ to buy a laptop. What is Luisa's bank balance at the end of the day on Tuesday?",
  "worked_solution": "To find Luisa's bank balance at the end of the day on Tuesday, we subtract the amount of money Luisa spent on the laptop from the starting balance, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\[math] 173.25 - \\[/math] 250.70 = -\\[math] 77.45\n$$\n\nTherefore, Luisa's bank balance at the end of the day on Tuesday was $-\\[/math] 77.45.$",
